method.description:
Loads and parses a YAML file from the given [param path]. Returns a [YAMLResult] containing either the parsed data or error information.
If [param security] is provided (a [YAMLSecurity] instance), it will be used to validate resource loading. Otherwise, the default security settings (see [method allow_resource_path], [method block_resource_type], [method reset_security]) will be used.
If [param detect_style] is [code]true[/code], the method attempts to detect and store style information from the input YAML. This style can be retrieved using [method YAMLResult.get_style] and used with [method stringify] or [method save_file] to preserve formatting when modifying and re-serializing the YAML.
[codeblock lang=gdscript]
var result = YAML.load_file("res://data/config.yaml")
if result.has_error():
    print("Error loading file: ", result.get_error())
else:
    var data = result.get_data()
    print("Loaded configuration: ", data)
[/codeblock]

Registers a custom script class for YAML serialization and deserialization. The [param script_class] must be a [Script] resource. The class should implement two methods:
- A serialization method (default name specified by [param serialize_method] that is called on an instance and returns a serializable [Variant] (e.g., a [Dictionary]).[br]- A static deserialization method (default name specified by [param deserialize_method], e.g., [code]static func deserialize(data)[/code]) that takes a [Variant] (the data from YAML) and returns a new instance of the class.
Once registered, instances of this class will be serialized with a YAML tag and deserialized back into objects of the correct type.
[codeblock lang=gdscript]
class_name Player extends Node

var name: String
var level: int

static func deserialize(data):
    if typeof(data) == TYPE_DICTIONARY:
        var player_instance = Player.new()
        player_instance.name = data.get("name", "")
        player_instance.level = data.get("level", 1)
        return player_instance
    # Custom errors can be returned using YAMLResult.error
    return YAMLResult.error("Player requires Dictionary to deserialize")

func serialize():
    return {
        "name": name,
        "level": level
    }

# In some setup code (e.g., _ready() of an autoload)
func _ready():
    YAML.register_class(Player) # Pass the Script resource

    var p = Player.new()
    p.name = "MyHero"
    p.level = 20
    var yaml_result = YAML.stringify(p)
    if !yaml_result.has_error():
        print(yaml_result.get_data()) # Will include !Player tag
        # Example: !Player {name: MyHero, level: 20}

        var parsed_result = YAML.parse(yaml_result.get_data())
        if !parsed_result.has_error():
            var deserialized_player = parsed_result.get_data()
            print(deserialized_player is Player) # true
            print(deserialized_player.name)   # MyHero
[/codeblocks]

Converts Godot [param data] to YAML and saves it to a file at the specified [param path]. Returns a [YAMLResult]. On success, the result's data will contain the YAML string that was written. On failure, it will contain error information.
If [param style] (a [YAMLStyle] instance) is provided, it will be used to customize the formatting of the YAML output. Otherwise, default formatting will be used.
[codeblock lang=gdscript]
var data_to_save = {
    "settings": {
        "volume": 0.8,
        "fullscreen": true
    },
    "player_profile": {
        "name": "Hero",
        "level": 5
    }
}

var result = YAML.save_file(data_to_save, "user://settings.yaml")
if result.has_error():
    print("Error saving file: ", result.get_error_message())
else:
    print("File saved successfully. Content written: ")
    print(result.get_data())
[/codeblocks]
